From: Plugg
Subject: [PATCH] wine-host: give plug-in threads a usable stack

A plug-in that did real work in IPluginBase::initialize() took the whole
Windows host process down, and the DAW then waited on a process that no longer
existed: "Plug-in host is not responding". Kilohearts, Native Instruments
Massive and XLN Addictive Keys all failed this way; the same plug-ins in the
same prefixes load under a plain Wine installation.

CreateThread() with a stack size of zero uses the executable's default, one
megabyte. Upstream never needs more because it starts the host directly with
the Wine loader, where the thread gets the Unix stack instead, normally eight
megabytes. Plugg starts it through Proton's `start.exe /exec` inside the
Steam runtime container, so the one megabyte is what a plug-in actually gets,
and initialisation runs off the end of it.

Wine reports the overflow as

  err:virtual:virtual_setup_exception stack overflow 3392 bytes addr ... stack 0x202c0 (0x20000-0x21000-0x120000)

where 0x20000-0x120000 is the megabyte. See diagnostics/host-stack.

The reservation is address space; pages are committed as they are touched, so
an idle thread costs nothing extra.

diff --git a/src/wine-host/utils.h b/src/wine-host/utils.h
index 75ace84..1d83516 100644
--- a/src/wine-host/utils.h
+++ b/src/wine-host/utils.h
@@ -67,6 +67,20 @@ win32_thread_trampoline(fu2::unique_function<void()>* entry_point);
  */
 class Win32Thread {
    public:
+    /**
+     * How much stack a plug-in's thread gets.
+     *
+     * `CreateThread()` with a size of zero takes the executable's default,
+     * which is one megabyte. Running the host directly under Wine gives its
+     * threads the Unix stack instead, usually eight, which is why this only
+     * shows up when the host is started through Proton's `start.exe /exec`
+     * inside a container. Plug-ins that do real work while initialising then
+     * run off the end of the stack and take the host process with them. The
+     * reservation is address space, not memory: pages are committed as they
+     * are touched.
+     */
+    static constexpr size_t stack_size = 16 * 1024 * 1024;
+
     /**
      * Constructor that does not start any thread yet.
      */
@@ -83,7 +97,7 @@ class Win32Thread {
     Win32Thread(Function fn, Args... args)
         : handle_(CreateThread(
                       nullptr,
-                      0,
+                      stack_size,
                       reinterpret_cast<LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE>(
                           win32_thread_trampoline),
                       // `std::function` does not support functions with move
